        "thought_text": "Consider the tiles divisible by both \\(a\\) and \\(b\\). These tiles can be painted either Red or Blue. To maximize the number of chocolates, we should paint all these tiles in the color that gives more chocolates per tile. Therefore, calculate the number of tiles divisible by both \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) (i.e., \\(\\text{lcm}(a, b)\\)), and then determine which color provides more chocolates when multiplied by this count. Use the larger value between the chocolates obtained by painting these tiles Red and Blue.",
